      "message": "For the success case, it\u0027s almost impossible to test because it highly depends on the carrier\u0027s network.\n\nFor the error case, the only error codes that are possibly testable are RADIO_NOT_AVAILABLE (i.e. device in airplane mode) and INVALID_ARGUMENTS.\n\nThe problem is that we have a very poor HAL definition (possible legacy behavior for 10+ years) https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/interfaces/radio/aidl/android/hardware/radio/network/IRadioNetworkResponse.aidl;l\u003d486\n\nIt does not specify in what kind of condition, the error code should be returned, but only all possible error codes.\n\nWhat would be your suggestion?",
